Am 29.04.2010 09:33, schrieb Jorge:
>>
>> The DSS2 driver (CONFIG_FB_OMAP2) does not detect any displays, on
>> loading the modules (or booting with them compiled into the kernel), I
>> get the following in dmesg:
>>
>> OMAPFB: omapfb_init
>> OMAPFB: omapfb_probe
>> omapfb omapfb: no displays
>> OMAPFB: free_resources
>> OMAPFB: free all fbmem
>> omapfb omapfb: failed to setup omapfb
>> omapfb: probe of omapfb failed with error -22
>>
>> No displays means no /dev/fb*. I tried loading the modules with
>>
>> # modprobe omapdss def_disp=dvi debug=y
>> # modprobe omapfb mode=dvi:1024x768MR-16@60 debug=y
>>
>> and without mode definitions. The really strange thing is that the
>> framebuffer works with the stock firmware from NAND, which has a rather
>> old kernel. My kernel config is attached.
>>
> 
> 
> Hi Thomas!
> 
> Did you found any solution for this problem?
> I'm using a 2.6.33 kernel based on linux-omap tree. I'm trying
> to get a working kernel with DDS2 and dsp-bridge support. Now,
> the DDS2 still not working.
> 
> Regards,
> Jorge

Hi Jorge,

I just pulled the latest commit from linux-omap
(104a77440f05430f29f9d3f4ecb88c1536819585), but the problem persists.
I've CCed the linux-omap list, I hope someone there knows how to fix or
at least properly debug this. For the record: I originally encountered
this problem in 2.6.33 (tagged release) from the linux-omap tree, on a
Gumstix Overo Fire. My current kernel config is attached.

Regards,
Thomas

